    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113-a15">

                <pb facs="0282" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg210"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 15 in No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Simms to Mr.
                            Lowell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>7 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Donegal Square South, Belfast</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1881-07-16"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            16, 1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Inclosed please find copy of letter from D.
                    Sweeney, Dundalk jail, to myself making inquiries as to the probabilities of his
                    speedy trial or release. I have no further information in the matter, and beg to
                    ask whether or not you have yet heard from Lord Granville.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM S. SIMMS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vice-Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
